===Etymology 2===
Frequentative of {{m|en|pote}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|pote|er}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|poteren}}, {{m|nl|peuteren||to poke, pry, search}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|putter}}, {{l|en|pouter}}, {{l|en|pudder}}, {{l|en|pother}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|British}} To act in a [[vague]] or unmotivated way; to fuss about with unimportant things.
# {{lb|en|British}} To move slowly or aimlessly. (Often {{m|en|potter about}}, {{m|en|potter around}}.)
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1923|author={{w|P. G. Wodehouse}}|title={{w|Leave It to Psmith}}|chapter=II| passage=He’s so dreamy and absent-minded. He '''potters''' about the garden all the time.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[poke]] repeatedly.

